# AMGSquant Print System - Cursor AI Rules

## Project Context
This is a monorepo project for a large-format printing house management system.
- E-commerce frontend with product configurators
- Backend API with production queue management
- Real-time pricing engine
- File validation (preflight)
- Warehouse management

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: Next.js 14 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Zustand
- **Backend**: NestJS, Prisma, PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ
- **Monorepo**: pnpm workspaces + Turbo

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Prefer functional components and hooks
- Use async/await over promises
- Error handling with try-catch
- Always add JSDoc comments for public methods
- Follow ESLint rules

## File Organization
- Group by feature, not by file type
- Keep components small and focused
- Separate business logic from UI
- Use index.ts for clean imports

## Naming Conventions
- PascalCase for components and classes
- camelCase for functions and variables
- UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants
- kebab-case for file names

## Best Practices
- Write unit tests for business logic
- Use DTOs for API validation
- Implement proper error handling
- Add loading and error states
- Optimize database queries
- Cache frequently accessed data in Redis

## Security
- Never commit secrets or API keys
- Validate all user inputs
- Use parameterized queries
- Implement rate limiting
- Use HTTPS in production

## Performance
- Lazy load images and components
- Implement pagination for large lists
- Use React Query for data fetching
- Optimize bundle size
- Use CDN for static assets
